# what is seen stored in `format` is a function of the program and a built-in, and held() leaves the built-in out of its type: a guess may go by the rest. A slot is held to all that arrives or to nothing:
# held to the one function, it would be left by every object that gets the other. So `format` is held to nothing. `name` beside it is held.
# -- source: a-slot-is-not-held-to-a-part-of-what-is-seen-stored.js
